<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ALGERIANS BOAST STRENGTH IN DEPTH.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALGERIANS BOAST STRENGTH IN DEPTH.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria, the country with probably the weakest team at the Alpine skiing world championships, can at least boast strength in numbers.</p>
<p>According to the official start list, the Algerians have twice as many skiers entered in Monday's opening men's super-G as France and the same number as the sport's superpowers, Austria and Switzerland.</p>
<p>But while Switzerland's Steve Locher starts first, Algeria's Kamel Guerri sets out 76th of 79.</p>
<p>By the time Ali Boukamoun, the fourth Algerian due to compete, makes his run, the winner will be long decided.</p>
</text>
